Lesson 2: Working With Text in HTML
Course: Web Development Basics
Grade Level: Beginners (Age 10+ or adult learners)
Duration: 45–60 minutes
Lesson Number: Day 2
Topic: Working With Text in HTML


1. Learning Objectives
By the end of this lesson, students will be able to:
•	Create paragraphs using <p>
•	Add line breaks (<br>) and horizontal lines (<hr>)
•	Use text formatting tags like <b>, <i>, <u>, <strong>, <em>Build a simple webpage containing properly structured text

2. Materials Required
•	Computer / Laptop
•	Online HTML Editors / IDEs:
o	Replit (https://replit.com)
o	CodePen (https://codepen.io)
o	JSFiddle (https://jsfiddle.net)
o	W3Schools Tryit Editor (https://www.w3schools.com/html/tryit.asp)
•	Slides (optional)
•	Teacher’s notes & sample code

3. Lesson Overview (Teacher Notes)
This lesson introduces students to the building blocks of website content:  paragraphs and text formatting tags. Students will learn how to organise information on a webpage and apply simple formatting like bold and italic. They will create a structured mini webpage with multiple headings and paragraphs.
4. Lesson Breakdown
	4.1 Warm-Up (5 minutes)
Share the screen and display a page with only text (try to include a page with a heading, subheading, bold text, multiple paragraphs, line breaks, etc.)
Now ask students
	What do you notice on this page?
	How do you think this webpage was created?
	Do you think all this text is written in one line or many lines?
	 If you had to create this webpage, what tools do you think you need?

	4.2 Recap & Transition from Day 1 (5 minutes)

Explain: Today, we will learn more tags that help us write actual content on a webpage. Before that, we will review the topics from yesterday quickly. 
	What is the purpose of <html>, <head>, <body>? 
	What is a heading tag? Why did we use <h1>  to <h6> yesterday?

	4.3 Teaching Headings & Paragraphs (15 minutes)
 
Basic Structure
 Guide students to type the code in any online HTML editor and run it to view the output.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Day 2 Practice</title>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>The Clean Park</h1>
 <p>Tyler asked his mom if he could ride his bike to the park. “As long as you wear your helmet when you are riding,” she said</p><p>When Tyler got to the park, it was filled with people holding garbage bags. A lot of his friends were there, and so were some of his teachers. His friend Bella
said, <br> “Everyone is pitching in and cleaning the park
today.” She asked Tyler if he would help. Tyler said,
“Sure,” and asked for a garbage bag. </p>
</body>
</html>

	Ask them about <p>, and <br>
	How its working? Ask them to add more <p> and <br> anywhere?
(wait for their response)

                               Then explain
	<p> - paragraph tag is used to write normal paragraphs, also remember 
<p> = new paragraph → new line + spacing (between lines)
	Line breaks: <br> (no closing tag)
<br> = only new line → no spacing (between lines)
	4.4 Text Formatting Tags (10 minutes)
               Make the kid type the following code 

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>About Me</title>
</head>

<body>
<h2>About Me</h2><hr>
<p>My name is <b>John</b>.</p>
<p>I love <i>coding</i>.</p>
<p>This is <u>important</u> text.</p>
 <p>I am <strong>John</strong>, a dedicated student who enjoys <em> making websites creatively</em>. </p>
</body>
</html>

	Ask them to identify the new tags
	Let the kid guess the usage (wait for the response, then explain)
	<hr> - horizontal rule, to divide sections, no closing tag
	<b> - make the text bold 
	<i> - to make the text italic
	<u> - to add underline
	<strong> -Also appears bold, used when the information is important or urgent 
	<em> - Makes text italic. Used when you want to emphasize a specific word in a sentence.
	Ask the kid the difference of <strong>&<em> with <b>&<i>
	<b> = bold (just design)
	<strong> = bold + important meaning
	<i> = italic (just design)
	<em> = italic + emphasis (stress the word)
	Ask the kid to change the locations of the tag and explore.

	4.5 Hands-On Coding (10 minutes)
Assign this challenge:
Ask students to create:
"About My Family" Webpage
Must include:
	One <h1> heading
	One <h2> or <h3> subheading
	One paragraph <p>
	Use at least 2 formatting tags such as <b>, <i>, <u>
Sample (Teacher Demo):

<h1>About My Family</h1>
<h3>Introduction</h3>
<p>My family has <b>four members</b>. We live in <i>Kochi</i> and love spending time together. </p>

	4.6 Hands-On Coding (10 minutes)
Challenge Students:
Create a webpage about “My Favorite Teacher”
Include:
	Heading
	Paragraph
	At least 3 formatting tags
	Use <br> at least once


5. Assessment (Exit Ticket – Quick Check)
Ask students to answer:
	Which tag is used for paragraphs?
	Write any two formatting tags.
	What is the difference between <h1> and <h4>?
	What does <br> do?
	What is the difference between <hr> and <u>?
	What is the difference between the following pair <b> -<i> & <strong> - <em>

